A||||4||Fiero5||Removing wing stantions?||||5||
Z||000000||Fiero5||09-24-2000||10:41 AM||||We want to put longer wing stantions on Marians Fiero2. I have the wing on my couch, and  I have started to take out the screws from the bottom of the wing that hold the stantion on the wing itself. Well, the screws are now half way out, and now they just spin. Now they won't tighten back up, or come out the rest of the way.<BR>Any thoughts?<BR>Thanks, Steve<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://kelleyfamilyfieros.homestead.com/files/sk2.jpg"> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||StuGood||09-24-2000||12:57 PM||||Sounds like you're halfway screwed   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">.  Sorry, bet that one doesn't sound so funny right now   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">.<P>I've got a Fiero spoiler with stanchions in my basement.  I don't have any reason to take it off its stanchions, and now you've scared me from trying it just for fun.  Thanks for the warning, though.<P>'Fit were me, I'd probably start by putting a mini pry bar under the screw head, gently pulling the screw out with the prybar as you turn the screw.  I can envision GM putting clip nuts (or some other low-cost nut element thingys) in there.  Obviously,  whatever they used, it came loose and is rotating with the screw, or it stripped out.<P>If you "guilt" me enough, I might try mine and let you know what I find.    <p>[This message has been edited by StuGood (edited 09-24-2000).]||||reg||4
Z||000002||Formula 18||09-24-2000||06:04 PM||||I took mine off once b/c the mounting holes started to leak into the trunk. I took off the risers off too b/c one was cracked. There are in witn a giant lag bolt tyoe screw. mine were a pain to get off but luckly it was cracked so 1/2 was alread off. hehe. BE CAREFUL when taking them off or you'll crack the wing too. <P>------------------<BR>Brian<BR> -88 Formula||||reg||1
Z||000003||2xsess||09-24-2000||06:14 PM||||The wing stantions screws go into a jacknut type thing. Your best bet would be to put a screwdriver in between the spoiler and the stantion to try to hold the jacknut still. Also try sparying penetrating oil on it.<P>Good Luck!!<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>85GT||||reg||1
Z||000004||wahoo4u||09-25-2000||03:21 PM||||little tricky is right.  i had to take some off a wing off a formula the stands were pretty busted up but the wing is still good.  got them off but they weren't fun.  Try the screw driver thing, seemed to work for me.  One question, how long of stands have you got and where did you get them?  I am looking for a set for mine but haven't found any yet.||||reg||10
